    "note": "Inspected aerial picture confirms coral-pink Baroque entrance wing, tall domed central tower, paired western roof towers, buff stone ranges and stepped garden terraces. Retained mapped castle/court rings and standard viewer PMTiles set approximate location, scale and entrance-facing orientation. The derivative reconstructs a working court at Y5, keeps terrace tops above coarse ground and moves the separate Powder Tower to its retained mapped position at native [88.89756493084487,47.64031319972397] with a coarse-ground footing. This review covers the castle/terrace model; separately modeled park buildings retain their own QA status. Anchor 16.291558848,50.842218729; heading 0.487948990682; standard PMTiles datum 392.7276846126304m. Floors are reconstructed and foundations extend below the coarse sampled ground. A mapped footprint mask replaces the castle, four tower parts and the separate Powder Tower only after the model loads. The independent pavilions and remaining park buildings use the host map. Preview uses the host terrain sample at the authored base; ground slope, facade azimuth and final site fit remain review items."
